WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.890
Speaker 1: The MAGA love affair with Elon
Musk seems to be coming to a sort of predictable

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.220
end.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:12.790
This all sort of got going around the Twitter
purchase that was simply not to be.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:19.340
Elon Musk of Tesla and SpaceX fame announced
that he wanted to buy Twitter and that he

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.950
had reached a deal with Twitter.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.279
I didn't believe it for a second.

00:00:22.279 --> 00:00:24.430
I didn't think he was going to buy Twitter.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.189
Then it sort of like nothing moves forward
for a little bit.

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:32.329
And Elon Musk announced that he's having some
concerns about the number of bots on the platform.

00:00:32.329 --> 00:00:38.760
This was after a whole flood of right wing
users came back to Twitter following right

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:39.760
wing accounts.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.230
On the heels of Elon Musk's announcement,
Musk started to say, Well, I'm not really

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:47.820
getting the data I want about the number of
fake users and bots.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.100
So I'm putting the purchase on hold.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:55.230
And I said at that point he was never going
to buy Twitter and he's not going to buy Twitter.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:58.660
And now Elon Musk actually says that he's
backing out.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.160
And it's, of course, not at all surprising.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:05.730
But in addition to this, Donald Trump and
Elon Musk are now publicly feuding in the

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.750
sense that Trump appears to be lying again
and Elon Musk seems to be telling the truth.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:17.070
Now, I think a lot of this was inevitable
in the sense that Elon Musk is basically a

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:20.450
self-centered opportunist, as are many tech
CEOs.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:25.380
I don't necessarily say that pejoratively,
although it could certainly be interpreted

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.510
as such.

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:31.470
And as a result, he and Donald Trump are now
not getting along well.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:37.270
During his rally at a in Anchorage, Alaska,
Donald Trump said the or actually, you know,

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:38.320
that's the wrong order.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.030
First and foremost.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:48.690
Donald Trump at his Anchorage rally said,
Elon Musk told me that he voted for me.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:51.730
But later said, I've never voted for a Republican.

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:53.720
And so therefore he must be a liar.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:58.850
Elon Musk responded to a report of that on
Twitter by saying It's not true, meaning it's

00:01:58.850 --> 00:01:59.850
not true.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.760
I ever told Trump I voted for him.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:05.540
So Trump getting called out for one apparent
lie.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:12.560
Then at the Anchorage rally, Trump going on
a rampage attacking Elon Musk, who he also

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.920
referred to as Leon Musk during the rally.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:20.170
Speaker 2: Another one of our highest priorities
under a Republican Congress will be to stop

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:23.700
left wing censorship and to restore free speech
in America.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:31.920
And go out, by the way, while I'm here and
sign up now for Truth Social.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.940
It's hot as a pistol and you see that?

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:36.360
I call that one, right, Leon?

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:39.350
I tell you what, Ellen.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:42.860
Ellen is not going to buy Twitter.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:46.540
Now, where did you hear that before?

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.590
From me.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:49.200
From a fake account.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.260
She says a lot of them.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.810
Now he's got himself a mess.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:56.120
You know, he said the other day, Oh, I've
never voted for a Republican.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.140
I said, I didn't know that.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.620
He told me voted for me.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:04.730
So he's another Bush, I guess, but he's not
going to be by and not going to be buying

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:06.100
it, although he might later.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.070
Who the hell knows what's going to happen?

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:09.420
He's got a pretty rotten contract.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:10.420
I looked at his contract.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:11.420
Not a good contract.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:12.420
Right.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.420
Speaker 1: Okay.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.290
So Breitbart highlighting that clip.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:22.170
And then Elon Musk responded, I don't hate
the man, but it's time for Trump to hang up

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:25.690
his hat and sail into the sunset.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:28.840
Democrats should also call off the attack.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:34.800
Don't make it so that Trump's only way to
survive is to regain the presidency.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:43.740
So the love affair between the MAGA people
and Elon Musk, predictably, predictably sunsetting.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.220
I think we could say.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:48.320
Now, let's talk a little bit about Elon Musk.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:52.240
I get a lot of people in my audience who are
Elon Musk fanboys.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.240
They love him.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.260
They love his products.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:55.690
They love everything.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:04:00.520
And then I hear from people who absolutely
hate Elon Musk and they see him as some right

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:04.080
wing extremist and all these different things.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:09.390
I well, it might not surprise you that much,
the same way that I don't really care about

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:12.990
or fall into the cult of personality among
politicians.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:14.900
I you know, I was a Bernie supporter.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.070
I wasn't part of the Bernie cult, so to speak.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:19.680
There's the Tulsi cult.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:21.321
Andrew Yang had a cult around him.

00:04:21.321 --> 00:04:25.060
Donald Trump is I just see these as people.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.280
Hopefully they do more good than harm.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:30.040
And if I think that they're the best option,
vote for them.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.130
But beyond that, I don't really get too sucked
into the personalities of it.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:36.430
And also in having met a lot of these people,
they're just normal people.

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:38.410
I mean, think about all the flaws.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:43.280
Everyone you personally know has they're just
normal people because they're normal people.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.090
All of these other people are as well.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.340
And much the same way on a business level.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:54.210
If you bet against Elon Musk, it doesn't seem
to be the best bet.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.970
Elon Musk has had a number of really successful
businesses I've disclosed.

00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:04.650
I bet on that when in 2015 I bought Tesla
stock and the stock went crazy, although now

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.530
it's down from its peak and whatever.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:11.570
It seemed that that was going to be a business
that would grow.

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:16.020
And it's by far the largest electric vehicle
manufacturer now in the United States.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.020
Great.

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:25.460
The degree to which Tesla has advanced the
electric vehicle development and normalization

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:26.699
is incredible.

00:05:26.699 --> 00:05:32.449
And the reason that every other vehicle manufacturer
now is scrambling to get more electric vehicles

00:05:32.449 --> 00:05:35.330
out there is because of the success of Tesla.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:36.510
That's a great thing.

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:40.560
Elon Musk also is just wacky on a lot of political
stuff.

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:46.470
The recent tweets about the the right is where
it's always been, but the left has become

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:47.470
extreme.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:48.630
That's just wrong as wacky.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.230
I don't know who gave him that idea.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.540
Just wrong.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:54.139
His recent thing about I'm now going to vote
for Republicans.

00:05:54.139 --> 00:05:55.750
I'm only voting for Republicans.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.260
Republicans are better for this, that or the
other reason.

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:58.260
He's just wrong.

00:05:58.260 --> 00:05:59.260
It's wacky.

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:00.260
It's completely wacky.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:01.400
Disagree with it completely.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:08.199
But at its core, the interpretation that makes
the most sense to me is Elon Musk has some

00:06:08.199 --> 00:06:10.690
bad ideas and some good ideas.

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:14.860
He uses tax law to his advantage as all of
these rich guys do.

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:20.300
He is a self-centered opportunist who at the
end of the day, wants what's best for himself

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:21.780
and for his companies.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.180
It's not a big surprise.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:26.880
We don't have to deify or demonize and just
recognize it for what it is.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:33.240
And all of that being said, he has never struck
me as a particularly reactionary guy.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:36.790
I think he's gotten sucked into right wing
Republican politics.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.720
Maybe it's hanging around with Rogan.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:43.990
I don't know what it is, but it seemed as
though the love affair between the MAGA people

00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:49.160
and Elon Musk was destined to end, and it
seems that it is indeed now ending, so hopefully

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:50.700
we can close the chapter on that.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:07:30.990
I don't believe he ever intended to buy Twitter
and I don't think he's ever going 

00:07:30.990 --> 00:08:00.719
to buy it.

